t, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/0d6728cdb8030be1cfcd2c819ef363032bf18ba80fd6bebe157f4022839e5d9a.png)\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/8f93d75dddcbee8927cb8baf990caaff8d1db2e875b497b17ef930bc7e97486c.png)\n\nNotice that\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/6a06c4ed3e01b53c334a640f492b405a66b9ff54e20c828f1d0a4c748051d5b0.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/6c4fc4d94830c32fa3b9c6c3371604fa398e7d701031114914de3b4a31714cd7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124241 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "656da168-af12-53c2-8add-2c82cf71b31c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "77bd52ee-454e-5794-83e5-991e7e4c13b5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5433" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/4a4616061123e27093fa73d17de5c81fb68527b83993cba4eec22fc0368fe364.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/c5e95c3c6c86e0719be77fc3db865c7a81995ef386ce7508ccef19ab307a783a.png) Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/e6c0ddd895406c6b79e4c520a7a4002060c917b51a6070f134be8c47dd63de0b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124242 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd0537f8-b091-580a-974e-8e928d54939d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9c8d9615-6a5d-5b6a-8735-b9b2f58331f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5434" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/8ddf6015972344b2afaccf34a63e5ae8c478f326a2b227c45499a1be168ce996.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff70614-02c3-5b27-a9a0-546bca3323e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121196} {:answer/id #uuid "c44392c8-0777-507c-9e5d-8811ed4f55e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121197} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ddd9b0-1ea2-59d1-850d-1a3a4c35bac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121198} {:answer/id #uuid "4d6fa4ad-83d6-587f-9dd7-5626e6670d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121199} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6f6773-2898-5c42-8dbd-6bad3a0b9913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c44392c8-0777-507c-9e5d-8811ed4f55e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121197} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69db9c1-a917-5eca-996c-9dbb2d21b306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c85c048e-abef-5c1d-9831-aaf3c4e70ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-12009" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot x+1\\cdot y \\\\ 1\\cdot x+0\\cdot y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cafc89cb-dd12-5c06-9d71-f7104b3b772e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327403} {:answer/id #uuid "1d237bf6-f7e8-5298-b897-4530d42c123e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327404} {:answer/id #uuid "622f0280-0ce5-58be-a01e-3b6f4a9af175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327405} {:answer/id #uuid "bccc3385-2676-5e2a-ab54-8cb1162ff994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327406} {:answer/id #uuid "f091aff8-baf5-58a8-9f64-26e95e9e9c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "622f0280-0ce5-58be-a01e-3b6f4a9af175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327405} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b41a73-5d2b-503e-8df3-cef50120bbef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0154d38-fc03-54ad-95de-4f6c4bbd8ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-168102" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot x+0\\cdot y \\\\ 1\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "656da168-af12-53c2-8add-2c82cf71b31c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c04f336-f728-53c1-b142-201c4cc187de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-z \\\\ x+y \\\\ y-z\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287581} {:answer/id #uuid "3179d5bf-a4c8-50f6-8c7b-8236129641a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287582} {:answer/id #uuid "2432f9e6-3b05-5b6c-9519-17ccf008e834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ x+y \\\\ y-z\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287583} {:answer/id #uuid "97c43184-bd7f-5195-8046-b27c8a4181f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y-z \\\\ x+y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287584} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3aa29a-9dcb-5c7d-8b40-5d0c4b6c7919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-z \\\\ -y-z \\\\ x+y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3179d5bf-a4c8-50f6-8c7b-8236129641a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c1a1f5-5179-5f0a-9f82-f962aa64a33a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b3d954a-970e-5df9-84d3-b38ba96cad0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-168105" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is \n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "979d6f25-f891-5724-a886-0897191fc0e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327410} {:answer/id #uuid "237ef57b-4d4b-5836-8e9e-389a61529a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/mat