ty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74a3cd4d-9215-5d06-bd68-798666c6d028" :question/math-academy-id "q-275661" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9y-3x \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea25fa61-cf54-53ee-b683-5a4c41aa52e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327420} {:answer/id #uuid "f55de872-732f-5a5e-a108-976ee39433c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f55de872-732f-5a5e-a108-976ee39433c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327421} :answer-field/id #uuid "77cb3746-d423-5a6a-a2c6-4d4fab6f48a5" :answer-field/ke