lank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14de7939-6a34-506f-af47-c50274dc11d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317066" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-5y+7x \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcb2e8ff-3121-5196-92e6-d918492b6934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcb2e8ff-3121-5196-92e6-d918492b6934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287611} :answer-field/id #uuid "35b4a8d7-1363-5534-b201-82e94429f588" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank}