n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6x \\\\ 9x+5y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd0537f8-b091-580a-974e-8e928d54939d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "863a0b0c-4d85-58df-b416-cd5d6ec9fd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123185} {:answer/id #uuid "b3cacdbc-5429-57d2-9e5f-b2ec6d40455a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123186} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd1e744-184d-5af9-96c1-2b2e70c46b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123187} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6c978f-3dc5-54e6-9361-6a4316c216b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123188} {:answer/id #uuid "6bba33f4-e59f-5d92-aad2-e34a964b0415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3cacdbc-5429-57d2-9e5f-b2ec6d40455a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123186} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5bbe309-e330-51ba-9760-7194eff2ef38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12f3bb3a-f83c-5bc7-89c6-1af5031ec24d" :question/math-academy-id "q-37881" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "656da168-af12-53c2-8add-2c82cf71b31c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e4de374-0eae-5cf1-a6f8-1ad931082e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-8x+4y \\\\ -3x+2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327491} {:answer/id #uuid "19ffcd9b-153b-5e49-af82-b4ea118b290b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4x-8y \\\\ 3x-2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327492} {:answer/id #uuid "46454ca9-47e6-5253-bd5b-62554bb9b168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x+y \\\\ x+2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327493} {:answer/id #uuid "9627a5fc-74ef-5f63-9c3c-420160f79a30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x+8y \\\\ -2x+3y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327494} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf77b95-72fa-5f33-b720-e2deec77ca31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x+8y \\\\ -3x+2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf77b95-72fa-5f33-b720-e2deec77ca31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x+8y \\\\ -3x+2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327495} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2416815-40b8-5f17-a2e3-1ed4786caa7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50910187-421e-57f5-ac10-958986331952" :question/math-academy-id "q-37921" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4x+8y \\\\ -3x+2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x+8y \\\\ -3x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd0537f8-b091-580a-974e-8e928d54939d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d9f91e8-67e8-520f-a2f9-3e19a08826aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327498} {:answer/id #uuid "0cefed82-a591-5dab-96ff-6541947be2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327499} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6435f0-f8fb-55d9-98d6-3a93a2230f7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327500} {:answer/id #uuid "476b9a87-2bbd-5c19-b97b-998fda5e7123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327501} {:answer/id #uuid "0b264bd8-c6d3-5363-ad67-3a2f9857c066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cefed82-a591-5dab-96ff-6541947be2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327499} :answer-field/id #uuid "447531af-908e-5b96-b8db-7a9c791d820c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0bbc0eb-9d91-592b-9084-4e86e05ea6ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-74935" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "625498ac-13fe-5c82-a219-b11a6574645b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327505} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa5d09a-a269-5417-8f4c-2011dfa7c921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327506} {:answer/id #uuid "2458d995-d090-55bb-b165-fa3012b60c56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327507} {:answer/id #uuid "f292bd4d-56df-5c2b-8506-f36d4c3ffb57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327508} {:answer/id #uuid "cedf16e9-f5f8-5511-b962-cbe434104651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "625498ac-13fe-5c82-a219-b11a6574645b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327505} :answer-field/id #uuid "6afa9463-6564-5a98-8773-b466467a6406" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f75e215-98a8-56cb-b6d1-346274712c51" :question/math-academy-id "q-74941" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+x \\\\ y-x\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ -x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bfa1bee-f474-5612-8af9-a7a21c8f37b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280031} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb7cd95-4329-5840-9f18-8c037422f4ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280032} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b9a623-668b-548a-a88b-66a166acaf21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280033} {:answer/id #uuid "20c0c215-6da8-556c-a5df-acb2d9d99207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280034} {:answer/id #uuid "bd48e46b-231b-5fdd-b920-223cf326b2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd48e46b-231b-5fdd-b920-223cf326b2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280035} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1c1220-b501-550d-b027-49a87b60f60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9c4fe27-fb6e-5544-9585-41aed92d912c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74944" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2y-5z+x \\\\ z-y+3x \\\\ -z-2x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $3\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
